  "id": "institutionalization",
  "term": "institutionalization",
  "definition": "Institutionalization is a form of contact with the criminal legal system in which a person is placed in an institution. In this context, it is treated as a relatively more severe legal-system contact and is associated with mental health symptoms such as anxiety, depression, hostility, and psychoticism.",
